  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this diagram",
      "items": [
        "Each box is a part of the system; colour = what kind (see the legend top-right).",
        "The top-right cluster is fine-tuning (adapters, train, registry); the lower area is the RAG pipeline.",
        "An arrow means 'talks to'; dashed = background/occasional. Click a box's SRC badge to see the code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Complete code map (every module)",
      "items": [
        "app/serve.py - answers a query end to end (retrieve then generate).",
        "app/model.py - loads the base model and attaches an adapter.",
        "app/lora.py / dora.py / quant.py - the LoRA, DoRA and quantized (QLoRA) adapter variants.",
        "app/train.py - fine-tunes an adapter; app/registry.py - stores and hot-swaps adapters.",
        "app/tasks.py - the task definitions training/eval use.",
        "app/rag/ingest.py + corpus.py - read source documents and build the corpus.",
        "app/rag/index.py - the chunk index; app/rag/search.py - hybrid retrieval over it.",
        "app/rag/fusion.py (RRF) + hyde.py + rerank.py - combine and re-rank candidates.",
        "app/rag/scope.py - the scope gate (what a caller may retrieve).",
        "app/rag/provenance.py - corpus versioning; app/rag/evalharness.py - quality measurement.",
        "app/rag/improve.py - a self-improvement (RSI) loop over the eval results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Guided tour - answering a question",
      "items": [
        "1. A user asks a question; serve runs the scope gate.",
        "2. Search retrieves candidates from the index (hybrid), then fusion + HyDE + rerank pick the best passages.",
        "3. The model generates an answer from those passages, optionally through a fine-tuned adapter.",
        "4. Separately: ingest builds the corpus/index; train produces adapters into the registry; eval + improve close the loop."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why it is built this way",
      "items": [
        "Retrieve first, then generate: the answer is grounded in real passages, not the model's memory.",
        "Adapters (LoRA/DoRA/QLoRA) fine-tune cheaply and hot-swap, so one base model serves many behaviours.",
        "The scope gate decides what a caller may retrieve, independent of the model.",
        "Provenance versions the corpus so an answer can be traced to the documents it came from."
      ]
    }
  ]
